# The loop around an await is an ordinary loop: the sum and the counter are values of the loop, and the await stands between the read of the element and the multiplication.
# Nothing enters the loop from outside at the await, so there is no switch over a state, and no variable lives in an object. The storage and the length of the array are read again behind the await.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="total" role=CoroutineBody
# CHECK-LABEL: steps by 1
# CHECK: Double b@[[sum]] = Phi(
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[k]] = Phi(
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[source]] = Load(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Reads:indexedContiguousProperties, {{*}}:GetArrayElement)
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[value]] = Patchpoint<CloningForbidden>(b@[[source]]:Register({{*}}isSuspension{{*}}:AwaitBySavingFrame)
# CHECK-NOT: isSuspension
# CHECK-NOT: Switch(
# CHECK-NOT: Reads:InternalFields
# CHECK: Double b@[[product]] = Mul(b@{{*}}, b@{{*}}, {{*}}:Mul)
# CHECK-NEXT: Double b@{{*}} = Add({{*}}b@[[product]],{{*}}:Add)
# CHECK: Load(b@{{*}}, offset = 8, ControlDependent|Reads:JSArray_butterfly
# CHECK: Int64 b@{{*}} = Add(b@[[k]], $1(
# CHECK-LABEL: end of loop
# The sum of the loop is the other operand. Which of the two stands first goes by their numbers, which differ from target to target.
# SUM-LABEL: name="total" role=CoroutineBody
# SUM-LABEL: steps by 1
# SUM: Double b@[[sum]] = Phi(
# SUM: Double b@{{*}} = Add({{*}}b@[[sum]],{{*}}:Add)
# SUM-LABEL: end of loop
